  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Georgia received $73.3M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 1,679 awards with an average award size of $43.6K. Obligations are down 99.3% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying activity with $59.2M in obligations, followed by the Department of Justice with $11.7M and the Department of Agriculture with $2.3M. TECHANAX LLC was the largest vendor with $7.6M in obligations, and FLIGHTWORKS INC and VETMED GROUP LLC each received $4.7M. Temporary Help Services was the top industry by obligations at $12.2M, followed by Ambulance Services at $9.4M and Other Computer Related Services at $8.1M. Historical fiscal-year totals show much larger annual activity: FY22 at $8.5B, FY23 at $11.1B, FY24 at $10.4B, FY25 at $11.7B, and FY26 at $9.9B. FY27 to date is $73.3M, reflecting the partial-year nature of current totals and the sharp year-over-year decline.",
